      "body": "Thanks for tackling this.\n\nI'm not sure about this approach with an atomic counter though. Would it make sense to instead have a shared mutex that would allow multiple consumers to take a read lock along with the cursor, which are then released in the destructor? Then only `ResizeCache` takes an exclusive lock? Just brainstorming here.",
