        "type": "User",
        "site_admin": false,
        "name": null,
        "patch_url": null
      },
      "body": "> it seems to force cursors to be destroyed on the thread that created them\r\n\r\n[Iterators alone are not thread-safe](https://github.com/bitcoin-core/leveldb-subtree/blob/bitcoin-fork/doc/index.md#concurrency) though, so we should not be passing them to other threads. I think in this case it should be fine.\r\n\r\n> `std::shared_mutex` may lose some of Core's lock checking\r\n\r\nDo we need this here? We do use a `shared_mutex` already in `SignatureCache` without any of the lock checking machinery.",
      "created_at": "2026-07-18T21:41:04Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-07-18T21:41:04Z",
